 the best choice because it follows the principle of frontier minimization. It flips a single internal disc without opening up too many new empty squares for the opponent. It avoids creating stable walls or taking dangerous squares (like X-squares), and it keeps the game grouped centrally, putting pressure on the opponent to find a valid response.\n\nAnswer: (G, 6)'}
