:\nThe move (D, 2) is the best choice because it maximizes the concept of mobility restriction. By flipping only a single piece and playing safely within the inner board (avoiding dangerous squares next to corners), I preserve the current board advantage where the opponent is walled in. This increases the likelihood that the opponent will be forced into a bad move on their turn.\n\nAnswer: (D, 2)'}
